/**
 * The format checker (`jsonschema._format`).
 *
 * `Draft7Validator(schema)` is built without a format checker, so formats are
 * *not* enforced while validating an instance.  `check_schema`, on the other
 * hand, does run with the draft 7 checker, which is why `"pattern"` values
 * must be regexes the engine can compile.
 *
 * Only the checks that need no third-party package are registered - the same
 * ones the reference interpreter ends up with.  `uri`, `uri-reference`,
 * `date-time`, `hostname`, ... silently pass there because their optional
 * dependency is missing, and so they are simply absent here.
